        "text": "Plot: The opera takes place in Egypt between 48-47 B.C.E., and follows Giulio Cesare as he pursues Pompeo (a military leader of the late Roman Empire) into Egypt. After capturing him, Pompeo's wife, Cornelia, begs Cesare to spare her husband. Cesare agrees, but tragically, he is too late; the Egyptians led by their king, Tolomeo, bring Cesare the head of Pompeo. Cornelia and Sesto (Pompeo's son) swear vengeance against Tolomeo. Meanwhile, Cleopatra (the sister of Tolomeo) is plotting to depose her brother, in order to become Queen of Egypt. In order to accomplish her plan, she colludes with Cornelia and Sesto to overthrow Tolomeo, and she seduces Cesare in order to enlist his help, too. Cesare falls in love with Cleopatra. However, a suspicious and jealous Tolomeo (now fighting to maintain his power) pursues Cesare, so Cesare must flee quickly. In an attempt to escape Tolomeo's army, Cesare purportedly drowns. Tolomeo then captures Cleopatra and Cornelia. In a plot twist, Cleopatra finds out that Cesare is not dead when he emerges to save her from her brother. Sesto then kills Tolomeo to avenge his father and liberate Cornelia. At the end of the opera, Cleopatra becomes the sole ruler of Egypt, Cornelia and Sesto pledge their allegiance to Cesare, and Cesare returns to Rome victorious.",
